<% content_for :page_title, "DecisionDesk — Eligibility Screening Demo" %>

<section class="hero container">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <div class="eyebrow">Configurable intake & decisioning</div>
    <h1>Professional eligibility screening for complex, evolving workflows.</h1>
    <p class="lead">DecisionDesk is a portfolio-grade demo of a business-facing intake platform. It guides applicants through a branching questionnaire, produces an eligibility outcome, and gives administrators a searchable dashboard of submissions and decision paths.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a href="/app" class="button">Launch Live Demo</a>
      <a href="#architecture" class="button button-ghost">See Architecture</a>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-microcopy">Now structured as a Rails project with JSON API endpoints, persistent demo data, and one-click reseeding for repeatable client demos.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-visual card">
    <div class="window-head">
      <span></span><span></span><span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="mock-screen">
      <div class="mock-sidebar">
        <div class="mock-pill active"></div>
        <div class="mock-pill"></div>
        <div class="mock-pill"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="mock-main">
        <div class="mock-stat-row">
          <div class="mock-stat"></div>
          <div class="mock-stat"></div>
          <div class="mock-stat"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-table"></div>
        <div class="mock-flow">
          <div class="mock-node active"></div>
          <div class="mock-node"></div>
          <div class="mock-node"></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="features" class="container section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div class="eyebrow">What it demonstrates</div>
    <h2>High-signal features for a client-facing portfolio.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid three-up">
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <h3>Branching intake</h3>
      <p>Applicants move through a conditional, multi-step questionnaire that adapts to prior answers and finishes with a clear recommendation.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <h3>Admin review</h3>
      <p>Administrators can search, filter, and inspect demo submissions, including a readable view of the exact decision path taken.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <h3>Resettable demo data</h3>
      <p>The demo can be restored to its seeded state with one click, making it ideal for repeated use by prospects without manual cleanup.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container section split-section">
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow">Suggested use cases</div>
    <h2>Broad enough to travel across industries.</h2>
    <p class="muted">The same intake-and-decision pattern can support benefits screening, operations triage, service routing, onboarding workflows, or internal review pipelines. That makes the project feel like a real B2B product rather than a toy app.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card bullet-card">
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>Eligibility and benefits screening</li>
      <li>Customer or partner intake</li>
      <li>Operations triage and routing</li>
      <li>Compliance or review workflows</li>
      <li>Admin dashboards and searchable submissions</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="architecture" class="container section">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div class="eyebrow">Architecture</div>
    <h2>Rails conversion pack.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid two-up">
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <h3>What this overlay includes</h3>
      <p>This package ports the validated prototype into Rails controllers, ERB views, API endpoints, and reusable service objects while keeping the same UI and screening behavior.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card feature-card">
      <h3>What stays simple on purpose</h3>
      <p>Demo persistence remains file-backed so the app is easy to run and reset locally. That keeps the portfolio story focused on workflows, UX, and architecture instead of setup overhead.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="container section">
  <div class="cta card">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Live demo</div>
      <h2>Try the screening flow and inspect the admin dashboard.</h2>
      <p class="muted">Use the seeded data, submit a new screening, and reset everything back to its initial state when you are done.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cta-actions">
      <a href="/app" class="button">Open Demo App</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
